[{:adr/real-repo-naming-6120 "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6120 (public, matching every prior vertical's own visibility), following the SAME cloud-itonami-isic-#### convention as all 115 prior/sibling actors, rather than the legacy J####-prefixed placeholder scheme. business-id updated from 'cloud-itonami-J6120' to 'cloud-itonami-6120' to match", :adr/related ["2607101800-cloud-itonami-gridtransmission-3510-blueprint" "2607101400-cloud-itonami-basicchem-2011-blueprint" "2607100300-cloud-itonami-missionops-9900-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 9900 ADR-0001s (106 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/test-status-6120 "kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 163 assertions, all green", :adr/id "2607102000", :adr/west-registration-deliberately-not-done-6120 "same established precedent as every prior fresh-blueprint build this scope: none of the cloud-itonami-isic-* repos are registered as west projects. cloud-itonami-isic-6120 follows suit -- no :extra-projects/west.yml entry", :adr/registry-field-replacement-6120 "the existing '6120' registry entry had its :repo, :business-id and :optional-technologies fields updated, and its explicit :maturity :spec override REMOVED so maturity/maturity-of now auto-derive :blueprint from the real :repo presence", :adr/all-deferred-candidates-resolved-6120 "with this build, EVERY candidate ever explicitly flagged as deferred in this scope has now been resolved ('3812' at ADR-2607101300, '3510' at ADR-2607101800, '6120' here) -- none remain outstanding. The next build will need a fresh candidate scan rather than picking up a flagged deferral", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 9, :spec 531, :total 646}", :adr/explicit-scope-note-6120 "the README's own text carries an explicit 'Scope note: licensed network operator, not a reseller' section naming cloud-itonami-isic-6190 directly and quoting i