oo -- this is a SHARED cross-cutting telephony-records capability (any telecom operator, reseller or infrastructure owner, needs E.164/CDR/SMS records), the same sharing pattern as :robotics being required fleet-wide -- NOT evidence of redundancy between the two verticals. Legacy placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J6120) confirmed via direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually existed", :adr/date "2026-07-09", :adr/blueprint-only-artifacts-6120 "published README.md, blueprint.edn, docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later, verbatim) -- SAME artifact set as every prior fresh-blueprint publication this scope. Deliberately NO src/test/deps.edn/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md", :adr/shape-honesty-check-6120 "'6120''s own registry-declared operating-states (:intake :provision :route :bill :support :audit) checked for shape-honesty concerns (the same discipline applied confirming '3510''s own new shape): genuinely consistent with EITHER business (a reseller routes calls over someone else's network; a network operator routes calls over its OWN network) -- the distinguishing fact is who owns the underlying infrastructure, not a different operational lifecycle, so no shape-honesty concern arises", :db/id -1, :adr/blueprint-count-updated-again-6120 "ADR-2607101800's own (is (= 9 (:blueprint m))) assertion updated to (is (= 10 (:blueprint m))), continuing the 'not a fixed invariant' framing ADR-2607100500 established. Added a live-state corroboration assertion ((is (= :blueprint (industry/maturity \"6120\")))) alongside the nine prior live-state corroboration tests and the synthetic-fixture-based unit test", :adr/next-steps-6120 "cloud-itonami-isic-6120 joins the nine prior fresh-blueprint picks as a tenth candidate available for a future :blueprint->:implemented promotion pass -- a nice round milestone for this :spec-authoring scope's own first ten builds. The underlying :spec-tier pool remains far from exhausted (530 remaining 4-digit-class candidates plus 3-digit-group entries)", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-6120 (community mobile network infrastructure operations) published as a fresh :blueprint"}]